' An ordinary new game, from the start screen, with the opponent the screen
' opens on. Nothing here names it, shortens a goal, or adds anything to
' anybody's pack.
'
' The player hires one man, waters the group at the Bearwoods spring and
' leaves him holding the place - which is what lets the opponent hold two,
' because it will not get more than one camp ahead of a human.
'
' What the opponent then does for itself: camps, hands its knife to the man
' it leaves so the place makes something, fills its own empty bottle at a
' spring - a bottle of water is one of the three things a mercenary takes -
' hires a second man with it, walks on, and camps a second place.
menuclick 160,100        ' the intro: a click goes to the start screen (IntroScene.cs:135-139)
menuclick 60,104         ' player one's slot opens: face 0, and Max for a name
menuclick 161,165        ' the rules toggle opens on extended; like the original
menuclick 163,54         ' START
mapclick 75,303          ' into New Sandez
clickon 248
hire
wait 20
esc
mapclick 61,355          ' sets out; the days on the road pass by themselves (v0.9.1 skips a travelling player's turns)
mapclick 61,355          ' walk in
wait 60
join                     ' one place held, which is what frees the opponent's second
esc
day
day
mapclick 61,355          ' back to the spring so the group keeps drinking
wait 20
mapclick 500,233
wait 20
esc
wait 10
esc
day
day
mapclick 61,355
wait 20
mapclick 500,233
wait 20
esc
wait 10
esc
day
day
mapclick 61,355
wait 20
mapclick 500,233
wait 20
esc
wait 10
esc
day
day
day                      ' their second camp goes up on this turn
save                     ' the cut, with the opponent's second camp standing
